# The Dockerfile's own COPY instructions are already explicit/minimal (see
# its comments), so this mostly matters for keeping the build context sent
# to the Docker daemon small and fast — belt and suspenders, not the only
# thing preventing something unwanted from ending up in the image.

node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/deploy
**/data

.git
.github
.claude

*.md
docs/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.db
*.db-journal

# Never bake real streamer data into an image, even by accident.
relay/data/
